{"name":"Barricade","hex":"#84623e","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"barricade","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A barrier constructed across a road, especially as a military defence","An obstacle, barrier, or bulwark."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To close or block a road etc., as, or using, a barricade.","To keep someone in (or out), using a blockade, especially ships in a port."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/barricade"}],"entries":[{"title":"Barricade","blocks":[{"text":"Barricade is any object or structure that creates a barrier or obstacle to control, block passage or force the flow of traffic in the desired direction. Adopted as a military term, a barricade denotes any improvised field fortification, such as on city streets during urban warfare. These may also include crowd control devices—like temporary traffic barricades, pedestrian barricades, and anti-vehicle barriers—all of which have also been used in the course of urban protests, counterinsurgency operations, and military operations on urban terrain."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Police_Barricades_at_Plaza_de_Mayo_Buenos_Aires.jpg/330px-Police_Barricades_at_Plaza_de_Mayo_Buenos_Aires.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barricade"},{"title":"Barricade (2012 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Barricade is a 2012 Canadian psychological horror film directed by Andrew Currie. The film stars Eric McCormack. The film was released on September 9, 2012. It is the first film entirely produced by WWE Studios to not feature a wrestler in any way. It was widely panned by critics and audiences"}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/71/Barricade_2012_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barricade_(2012_film)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedi